SUMMARY:Algonquin Park Backcountry Canoe Trip: Magnetawan Loop (4 Days / 3
  Nights)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Canoe Trippers\n**Dates:** July 31 – August 3\, 2026
 \n**Start/End Location:** Algonquin Park\, Magnetawan Lake Access Point (#
 3)\n**Total Distance:** \\~35 km (30 km paddling\, 5.25 km portaging)\n\n*
 *Experience Level:** Intermediate/Advanced. You must be capable of a 2.4 k
 m portage while carrying a canoe and/or full pack. Expect full paddling da
 ys with some longer carries — this is not a beginner trip.\n\n**Costs & 
 Payment:**\n\n* **Permit:** $33 + HST ($11/night) per person for the backc
 ountry permit.\n* **Parking:** Total cost for parking fees will be split e
 qually.\n* **Deposit:** An upfront e-transfer is required to secure your s
 pot on the permit. Your RSVP is not confirmed until payment is received.\n
 \n**Itinerary:**\n\n* **Day 1 (July 31): Magnetawan AP to Queer Lake**\nTo
 tal Distance: 12\\.5 km \\| Portages: 130m\\\, 290m\\\, 450m\\\, 180m\n* *
 *Day 2 (August 1): Queer Lake to Daisy Lake**\nTotal Distance: 10\\.5 km \
 \| Portages: 2\\\,435m\\\, 450m\\\, 135m\n* **Day 3 (August 2): Daisy Lake
  to Ralph Bice Lake**\nTotal Distance: 6\\.7 km \\| Portages: 420m\\\, 50m
 \\\, 290m\n* **Day 4 (August 3): Ralph Bice Lake to Magnetawan AP**\nTotal
  Distance: 5\\.4 km \\| Portages: 290m\\\, 130m\n\n**Logistics\, Gear & Di
 sclaimer:**\n\n* **Self-Reliance:** This is not a guided tour. You are ful
 ly responsible for your own safety\, navigation\, preparation\, and gear (
 canoe\, paddle\, PFD\, tent\, sleeping system\, food\, and water filtratio
 n).\n* **Communication:** Cell service is unreliable/non-existent along th
 is route.\n* **Coordination:** Coordinate in the event chat to share tande
 m canoes\, carpooling\, and rental costs.
